ENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"French, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"Trbe4JX-oLHrrVVPcv0wog","review_id":"38wXOXGno-7N_tFP_aVEww","date":"2018-07-30T21:44:32","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9515487551689148,"text_excerpt":"I loved this place! We went for Sunday Brunch. I made reservations ahead of time for 11.30am, but there was room available when we arrived. Great service!! I really wanted to seat outside, but there was a chance of rain, so the patio was closed. The staff was very accommodating, and per my request, they seated us closed to a window overlooking the patio on the bar area. About 15min later I wanted a table closer to the Jazz Band on the dinning area, and they were patient and nice enough to move us to the dining room. I have to admit that the food surprised me in a good way. I am usually not a fan of the French Quarter restaurants, but this one was on point. My favorites were the crawfish g..."},{"business_id":"Trbe4JX-oLHrrVVPcv0wog","review_id":"1XU6_JT9RPzGczE5l7UBow","date":"2019-02-14T02:28:14","stars":4,"text_representativeness":0.9457607269287109,"text_excerpt":"Another historic big player in the Nola fine dining scene - I decided to give Broussards a try for their jazz brunch. The décor was certainly elegant but didn't feel stuffy. Plus, who doesn't love bottomless mimosas or sparkling rosé? We were one of the last seatings on MLK Jr Day, so there were not many people dining. There was one huge party, and I assume the wait staff was a little light, because it did take some time for our orders to be taken and arrive. The jazz musicians were also on their last set and packed up while we were still dining - it would have been nice if they could have stayed a little longer. We pretty much only had one waiter for our table (as opposed to a pair or a ..."},{"business_id":"Trbe4JX-oLHrrVVPcv0wog","review_id":"52exyvN4Yn-tjrJa_Ddocw","date":"2016-07-13T21:29:53","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9435139894485474,"text_excerpt":"This is probably THE best brunch spot in New Orleans. Came here about two months ago for brunch with the ladies. We were originally seated inside, but requested to move to the courtyard to enjoy the nice day before NOLA weather became unbearable. The hostess set up a table and moved us promptly. They serve bottomless mimosas, and let me tell you they are not at all skimpy with the pouring. They have tubs of cava bottles chilling in the courtyard and seeing as we were serious drinkers, brought us the big glasses instead of the champagne coupes. I had all appetizers, including an amazing crab and endive salad. We enjoyed the jazz band, and once we had paid our bill, we moved to a shady seat..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"Trbe4JX-oLHrrVVPcv0wog","photo_id":"yqvGRYOTMauwE7_oIc9vCw","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/yqvGRYOTMauwE7_oIc9vCw.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.868105411529541},{"business_id":"Trbe4JX-oLHrrVVPcv0wog","photo_id":"O4EmidF2DZKjAvCoRSan3w","label":"food","image_url":"/photos/O4EmidF2DZKjAvCoRSan3w.jpg","vi